  "identity": "University of Twente Civil Engineering BSc, English, 2026–2027",
  "curriculum": "The University of Twente 2026–2027 EER B1.1 and B2.3–B2.7 and Appendix A establish an English-taught 180 EC BSc, with four mandatory 15 EC modules in each of the first two years. Each includes an integrated project. The third year has a 30 EC approved minor followed by a 30 EC graduation semester. The graduation semester includes Production of Knowledge (5 EC), the thesis proposal (10 EC) and the supervised bachelor assignment and evaluation (15 EC). Appendix A resolves the curriculum webpage’s extra digit in the Calculus 1B code: 202001196. The two sources agree on credits.",
  "progression": "EER B2.5 and the official entry page require completion of modules 1–8 before graduation as the normal rule. Narrow concurrent exceptions allow up to 4 EC in specified modules. This sample uses the ordinary sequence. The minor has a separate concurrent outstanding-credit rule and its own eligibility or approval requirements. Module 11 precedes Module 12, with the assignment starting in week 9 of Module 11 and continuing across the boundary. EER B4.1–B4.3 specifies a 15 EC supervised assignment normally in an external civil engineering organisation, with final report, evaluation and examination.",
